<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ballarpur</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ballarpur is a town on the Wardha river in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chandrapur">Chandrapur</a> district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharashtra">Maharashtra</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. It served as a capital of the Gond kingdom of Chanda before the court moved to Chanda (Chandrapur) in the 15th or 16th century, and its fort survives on the riverbank. It is now an industrial town known for paper making and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coal">coal</a>.</p></div>
